A||||16||jerpro||horrible gas mileage||||1||
Z||000000||jerpro||12-21-2000||05:44 PM||||I bought the 84se in october and since then it is doing horrible gas mileage. <BR>The car is in excellent condition (stored winters) and it pulls like a deamon. <BR>I have totally serviced the engine (i think).<BR>The car runs great (i think. this is my first fiero 4cyl)<BR>I am doing around 17-21 mpg and I have heard these cars should be better.<BR>do you thinnk the last owner did something to the car?<BR>He told me he had replaced the computer (he works for gm electric dept. and did it himself)<BR>any suggestions?<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||maninblack||12-21-2000||05:46 PM||||maybe your car is running too rich?have you check to see if there are any code(s).There<BR>could be a few combination to have poor gas milage||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||12-21-2000||05:59 PM||||If it "pulls like a demon"...it's probably got a 4.10 final drive. This was put on the car to give it performance, but at the expense of fuel economy.<P>You're in Grand Rapids, so it's cold...that also kills gas mileage. Check your thermostat  to see if it's a 195...this will help economy in the winter. <P>Also replace the oxygen sensor if you haven't already and switch to a 5W30 or lighter oil. The Mobil 1 0W30 really helps with cold starting and gas mileage. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||HAGS||12-21-2000||06:26 PM||||Just be glad you dont have my 10 mpg 4 cyl...I think it about time I chucked it for a V-8...lots of problems yesterday, my air filter assembly ripped one of the screws from the TBI off and now smoke comes out of the TBI...I can only give it very little gas before it starts to pop and hit the back...I can do about 30 up hills and 50 down hill, my 0-30 time is about 15 seconds.  I had to goto the post office today and it starting knocking, im about to try the Valvoline Complete Fuel System Treatment that I got to see if that helps at all...I dont even call my Fiero a car anymore...its just an $800 AM/FM radio with AC||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-21-2000||08:45 PM||||Alot of the 84's had those 410 finals. Nice off the line but beats the hell out of fuel eco. Tire size & inflation will affect it too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jerpro||12-22-2000||12:10 PM||||what are the pluses of having the 410 ratio?<BR>In  what way does it differ from other 84's?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||deceler8||12-22-2000||12:29 PM||||The 4.10 trans was a performance enhancing option...it gets you off the line quickly and to 60 faster than the standard "economy" version...but it also limits top speed and probably cuts 25% off the 2.5 fuel economy.<P>It was mainly used as there was no larger engine option in 1984.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||12-22-2000||12:37 PM||||Hey Hags, it sound like your motor mounts and dogbone are shot.  Ignore that and you will be facing real damage to the intake and TB and exhaust system.  SOunds like things are starting to tear up already from your description.<P>Take care of the Fiero and they will usually take care of us.  Ignore things when they go bad and things only get worse.  Not really fair to blame the car if we don't fix problems when they happen.<P>Take care and happy holidays...<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000008||HAGS||12-22-2000||07:26 PM||||I replaced all 3 mounts, im about ready to go poly, right now I have the whole TBI unit out for cleaning although it wasnt too bad, even on the bottom, other than not being able to give it any gas it also knocks now like a diesal truck.||||reg||1
Z||000009||jerpro||12-29-2000||09:25 PM||||deceler8, do you know the stats of the 4:10 transmission upgrade. (0-60 how many secs... and at what speed is it limited... etc..) thanks||||reg||1
Z||000010||William Federle||12-29-2000||09:36 PM||||I have a 1984 SE and I get from 27 MPG in the winter to 32 MPG in the summer. I also<BR>have the 4.10 final ratio transmission. My engine turns about 3000 RPM at 60 MPH. <BR>One thing though - my engine has so little compression that it won't hold the car on my driveway without the help of the parking brake. It doesn't smoke when it warms up (yet) but I'm sure that your car has a tighter engine from your statement of it pulling well. I mean, the engine being tight might partially explain the reduced MPG.||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||12-29-2000||10:53 PM||||DO a compression test on it. Don't use holding on a hill as a test. The engine is not ment to be a parking brake. They gave you a lever on the floor for that. <P>Even with perfect compression the engine will leak down and roll down the hill. The gear you leave it in will also effect this.||||reg||1
Z||000012||jerpro||12-30-2000||08:55 AM||||here comes the million dollar question....<BR>How do you do a compression test?<P>(MAN!!!! I can't wait to get into that automotive class in a week!!!!!)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||deceler8||12-30-2000||10:46 AM||||Another thing to check is the air preheater hose that leads from the "stove" on the exhaust manifold to the air cleaner.<P>In very cold weather, if this is missing, it will kill fuel economy and drivability.<P>Make sure it's there and that it doesn't have any holes or cracks in it. <P>Also be sure the Thermac door in the air cleaner is closed at startup so the engine is receiving warm air during warmup.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Seanh||12-30-2000||02:05 PM||||You buy a compression guage at an automotive store, remove all your spark plugs, screw in the compression guage fittings and connect to compression guage. Make sure nothing is in the way of the belts and crank the car over for about 4 seconds. Check your guage and record its readings. Do this for all the cylinders. Also note the car should be at normal operating temp. before doing the compression check. One other thing, you think thats bad mileage??? My Fiero (86 GT) gets 9-11 mpg and my `85 Big Bronco gets about 2-4 MPG highway. Less then 1 mpg when off-roading. (Also has 266K miles on the engine)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000015||jerpro||01-09-2001||06:55 PM||||was the 4.10 also in the autos or only the manuals?||||reg||1
